@startuml
' purpose: OpenCode-only categorized seed progress and the measured history-processing startup bottleneck
' covers: defs/opencode/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/opencode/README.md
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-await-seed
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-seed
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-opencode-preflight
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime
' covers: packages/lib/opencode_startup.py
' covers: packages/lib/test_opencode_startup.py
' covers: packages/lib/test_opencode_runtime.py
' covers: internal/contract/opencode_seed_progress_test.go
' covers: e2e/opencode_seed_progress_test.go
' Surface: _spec/packages/lib/opencode-seed-progress-wireframe.puml
' Existing release semantics: _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml
' Credential policy proposal: _spec/_paradigms/opencode-oauth-persistence.puml
' Five-second storage redesign: _spec/_plans/opencode-versioned-history-storage.puml
'
' SHIPPED: only the OpenCode image enables PROVEO_SEED_PROGRESS=1 by default.
' Other harnesses retain their current silent wait unless separately configured.
' Producer functions publish one atomic category/detail line to /dev/shm/proveo-seed-status.
' PROVEO_SEED_STATUS_FILE overrides the path for isolated tests and diagnostics.
' Both producers write the same category/detail to stderr for the sbx startup log.
' Categories reuse internal/ui/ui.go: credentials, workspace, setup, interface, starting.
' Labels describe operations, not credential values, email identities, tokens or secrets.
' Status write failure never aborts the seed; consumers fall back to a generic starting label.
'
' Consumers draw immediately while waiting and rotate ASCII | / - backslash at 5 Hz on a TTY.
' Pipe/dumb-terminal output writes plain step changes and a five-second elapsed heartbeat.
' All progress goes to stderr so --cwd and native JSON/stdout remain machine-readable.
' Clear the transient row before native exec, timeout, refusal, or shell termination.
' Do not hide the cursor or start an orphanable spinner subprocess.
' Shell and Python waits retain their existing release markers, deadlines and refusal checks.
' OpenCode runtime --sanitize/--recover must never wait for the marker they help release.
' The ordinary OpenCode lifecycle wait keeps displaying producer updates after the shell's 30s timeout.
' The preflight completion wait reads the same status while post-release toolchain setup continues.
' Instruction release remains before toolchain installation; progress does not delay native launch.
'
' OBSERVED original boot 2026-10-09: dispatcher start 17:27:32Z; instruction marker birth 17:29:00Z.
' That is approximately 88s to the first release; seed-done marker birth was 17:29:25Z.
' The original wait emitted no output for its initial 30s; the old runtime emitted one generic wait line.
' Canonical DB: 878718976 bytes; legacy DB: 1763418112 bytes; legacy WAL: 378648632 bytes.
' Startup logged divergent history, followed by offline sanitize failure on SQLite sidecars.
' The removed implicit merge snapshotted both histories and computed SQL digests before detecting divergence.
' sanitize_host_stores then restages both histories and republishes the canonical snapshot.
' Failed legacy publication does not remove the cost of its preceding backup and sanitization.
'
' READ-ONLY PROFILE on source stores; destinations were disposable private copies, then removed.
' No source checkpoint, credential inspection or live-database publication was performed.
' Canonical credential-free backup: 7.632s; legacy credential-free backup: 14.276s.
' Legacy SQL history digest: 12.145s; canonical SQL history digest: 2.352s; digests differed.
' Canonical sanitize restaging: 7.255s; canonical sanitize publication: 7.814s.
' Legacy sanitize restaging: 11.776s; measured operation total: 63.250s.
' Sanitized canonical sample: 287 session_v2 rows, 7704 session_message rows, 214531 pages, zero free pages.
' Sanitized legacy sample: 95917 event rows, 429251 pages, zero free pages.
' INFERENCE: repeated large snapshots and SQL serialization dominate the observed pre-release delay.
' The profile excludes migration path rebasing, some inventory/copy overhead and original cold-cache effects.
' It does not reconstruct every second of the historical 88s boot or establish a startup speedup.
' This change adds progress and phase timings; it does not optimize or modify credential publication.
' Follow-up candidates: avoid repeated unchanged divergent-store comparisons; reduce duplicate snapshots;
' preserve exclusive lifecycle ownership before checkpointing WAL destinations, never delete WAL blindly.
' FK (manual syllables): STATUS 10.3 (30w/51s); WAIT 12.0 (29w/54s).
'
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title OpenCode seed progress — categorized status, unchanged launch gates

participant "proveo-seed" as SEED <<app>>
participant "proveo-opencode-runtime\n--check-prepared" as GATE <<app>>
participant "entrypoint-lib.sh\nproveo_seed" as LIB <<app>>
database "proveo-seed-status\natomic category/detail" as STATUS <<db>>
participant "await-seed / runtime / preflight\nwaiting consumer" as WAIT <<app>>
actor "Executor\nterminal or captured stderr" as OP

SEED -> STATUS : starting: preparing OpenCode seed
SEED -> STATUS : credentials: checking prepared V2 history
SEED -> GATE : bounded metadata/owner validation; no bulk sanitization
GATE -> SEED : prepared or explicit maintenance required
WAIT -> STATUS : read current category/detail
WAIT -> OP : Waiting for seed + step + elapsed + spinner
SEED -> LIB : seed configuration
loop workspace, setup, credentials, interface
  LIB -> STATUS : current category/detail
  LIB -> SEED : matching seed-log label
  WAIT -> STATUS : read current category/detail
  WAIT -> OP : refreshed step
end
LIB -> STATUS : starting: releasing agent
LIB -> WAIT : instruction marker
WAIT -> OP : clear transient row; native handoff
LIB -> STATUS : setup: toolchains and dependencies
LIB -> STATUS : starting: seed complete
LIB -> SEED : return; write completion marker

note over STATUS
  Write status as one consistent atomic update
  so readers never show half-written step labels.
  Describe the current credential task without
  placing secret values in the status file or
  startup log.
end note

note over WAIT
  Show categorized seed steps without changing
  the release owner or existing startup timeout.
  Preserve stdout for machine output and clear
  terminal animation before handing control to
  the native client.
end note
@enduml
